            <ArticleTitle>Behavioural changes in the rat following infection with varicella-zoster virus.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2433-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Following the establishment of a chronic varicella-zoster virus infection in the rat, behavioural allodynia and hyperalgesia were observed in the injected, but not the contralateral hind limb up to 33 days post-infection. This model may prove useful in investigating mechanisms involved in the establishment of post-herpetic neuralgia.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
